frpc for Debian
---------------

The frpc service is installed but not enabled or started: upstream's
example configuration points at a server on localhost. Set serverAddr,
auth.token and your proxies in /etc/frp/frpc.toml first, then check it and
start the service:

  frpc verify -c /etc/frp/frpc.toml
  systemctl enable --now frpc

frpc runs as the frp user. For more than one client configuration,
frpc@<name>.service reads /etc/frp/<name>.toml.

"systemctl reload frpc" (frpc reload) and the admin web UI need frpc's
admin API: webServer.addr and webServer.port (and user and password) in
the configuration. frpc logs to the journal unless log.to names a file;
files in /var/log/frp are writable for the service.

The full configuration reference is
/usr/share/doc/frpc/frpc_full_example.toml.
